WEBVTT

00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:14,610
Okay, so we're going to talk about what I call three phases of chronic line.

00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:19,150
So I know anybody that's had chronic line, you well educated yourself.

00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:21,710
There's a lot of information on the internet.

00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:25,950
You study a lot about chronic line, you feel like you've got a handle on it, but you're

00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:29,110
here because maybe there's something else you could learn.

00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:32,950
So I apologize in advance if you already know everything that I'm going to say.

00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:37,350
But I'd be willing to bet there's going to be something I'll say that will be an enlightenment

00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:39,190
to somebody here.

00:00:39,190 --> 00:00:45,590
So the first phase of Lyme disease is that acute infection.

00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:50,310
So we're not going to get into, is it the Borrelia or the Doropy, is it the colon

00:00:50,310 --> 00:00:51,310
infections, is it what?

00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:56,190
Because I've never seen a chronic line patient that hasn't had multiple colon infections.

00:00:56,190 --> 00:01:00,950
So right now we're going to talk about how to deal with these different phases of chronic

00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:06,710
line, how ideal with them in our office, and the treatments that I would suggest in

00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:09,910
the doc suggest for a chronic line patient.

00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:15,950
Number one in the acute infection stage, I always recommend antibiotics.

00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:21,070
The problem is that we don't always know that if we've been acutely effective.

00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:26,990
So not everybody gets this perfect bull's eye reaction, not everybody gets this flu-like

00:01:26,990 --> 00:01:27,990
symptoms.

00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:32,830
And you only recognize that you have Lyme disease when you're already getting a chronic

00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:34,710
or later stage.

00:01:34,710 --> 00:01:37,190
That's the difficulty.

00:01:37,190 --> 00:01:44,150
And thank you to the representative here that's getting things passed so that patients can

00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:49,510
be in a acute phase and get into the doctor and say, I think I have Lyme disease, I got this

00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:53,270
bull's eye rash, I got this fever, I feel super sick, it's in the middle of the summer,

00:01:53,270 --> 00:01:58,230
I don't think I have the flu, and the doctors aren't quite so afraid of giving them an antibiotic

00:01:58,230 --> 00:01:59,230
prescription.

00:01:59,230 --> 00:02:04,670
Because as you know, if they go, oh, we got to run the Lyme test, which is only about 30% after

00:02:04,670 --> 00:02:08,150
it's the first place and they run the Lyme test and it takes three weeks to get back.

00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:11,910
You already may have moved past the acute stage.

00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:17,390
The acute stage of a Lyme infection is when it is still in a bacteria, it's always a bacteria,

00:02:17,390 --> 00:02:24,190
but when it's in a true bacterial phase, a bacteria is the only thing that can be killed by an antibiotic.

00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:30,030
The reason why viruses can't be killed by antibiotics is because viruses are smaller and they have

00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:33,830
the ability to go inside of a cell.

00:02:33,830 --> 00:02:42,430
So normally, if any pathogen, that's anything that you're infected with, goes inside of a cell.

00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:47,310
The cell puts up this marker on the outside of the cell, that tells the immune system that

00:02:47,310 --> 00:02:52,510
it has been infiltrated and then a macrophage or some white blood cells, it's going to surround

00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:57,270
that cell and destroy that entire cell and thereby kill that virus.

00:02:57,270 --> 00:03:01,550
So in an environmental infection, you need an immune response to kill it because if you

00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:04,830
take antibiotics, antibiotics aren't going to kill a virus.

00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:09,990
The problem with Lyme disease is that it's only killable with antibiotics if it's in that

00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:13,790
bacterial phase that hasn't yet gone inside of a cell.

